                <pb facs="0553" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1949v03/pg516"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On May 13 <hi rendition="#italic">Taegliche Rundschau</hi> published the text of
                    an election appeal by the secretariat of the German People’s Council for the
                    third German People’s Congress. The voting for delegates to the Congress took
                    place on May 15 and 16, and all five <hi rendition="#italic">Laender</hi> of the
                    Soviet zone and the eastern sector of Berlin registered majorities for the
                    single list of candidates. For the text of the election appeal and the results
                    of the voting, see Ruhm von Oppen, <hi rendition="#italic">Documents on
                        Germany</hi>, pages 393–395. The results of the voting are also printed in
                    G. N. Goroshkova, <hi rendition="#italic">Dvizheniye nemetskogo narodnogo
                        kongressa za edinstvo i mirnyi dogovor</hi> (Moscow, Izdatel’stavo Instituta
                    Mezhdunarodnikh, 1959) page 187.</p>
            </div>
